#lang saffron/bogus
;; saffron-lang-plan S1: an unknown reader under a known language is still an
;; unknown BASE.  `saffron/bogus` names no (language, reader) pair, so it takes
;; the same path `#lang foo` does rather than silently degrading to `saffron`
;; with the default reader -- a file that asked for a reader it did not get
;; would parse under semantics it did not ask for.
(println "hello")
